## Agent slot: W5-A — DOS-218

- **Title:** Substrate: migrate `get_entity_context` as first Read-category ability pilot
- **Linear:** https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-218 (fetch via linear MCP)
- **Output:** `.docs/plans/wave-W5/DOS-218-plan.md`
- **Wave plan section:** `.docs/plans/v1.4.0-waves.md` §"Agent W5-A — DOS-218 migrate `get_entity_context` (Read pilot)"
- **Reviewers (3 stacked):** accessibility-tester + architect-reviewer + codex-consult

## Things to be aware of

- This is the **Read pilot** — the first ability to run on the full W3/W4 substrate. Its job is to prove the pattern, not to add features. Parity with the legacy command on bundle-1 is the bar, not improvement.
- The legacy surface is `get_entity_context_entries` at `src-tauri/src/commands/workspace.rs:1237`, which calls `crate::services::entity_context::get_entries`. There is also `get_entity_context_for_prompt` at `src-tauri/src/intelligence/user_context.rs:89-108` used inside intelligence prompts. Understand both before designing the ability.
- **Read category** per ADR-0102: pure read, no mutations, no publish, no side effects. The ability returns data; it does NOT update the DB, trigger enrichment, or emit signals.
- The ability must produce full **Provenance + SubjectAttribution + `source_asof` + Trust band + composition** per the W5 done-when criteria. These come from W3-B (DOS-211), W3-C (DOS-7), W3-G (DOS-299), and W4-A (DOS-5) respectively. Read those L0 plans in `.docs/plans/wave-W3/` and `.docs/plans/wave-W4/`.
- `source_asof` fields on entity context entries — these are user-written notes, not AI claims. Understand how `ItemSource`/`SourceAttribution` applies to user-authored content vs AI-authored content.
- W3-H (DOS-300) adds `temporal_scope` + `sensitivity` to claims. Entity context entries have their own sensitivity implications (user-authored = higher privacy expectation).
- Parity test: the ability output should be equivalent to what the legacy command returns for bundle-1 test fixtures. Any delta is a regression until intentionally accepted.

## Files owned

- `src-tauri/src/abilities/get_entity_context/` (new directory + mod.rs + types.rs + input.rs + output.rs)
- Parity integration test against legacy `get_entity_context_entries` command
- Bundle-1 fixture seed data (coordinate with W6-A; stub if W6-A hasn't landed)

## Key code surfaces to grep

- `src-tauri/src/commands/workspace.rs:1237-1245` — `get_entity_context_entries` (the command being replaced)
- `src-tauri/src/services/entity_context.rs` — the service layer behind the command
- `src-tauri/src/intelligence/user_context.rs:89-130` — `get_entity_context_for_prompt` (used in intel prompts)
- `src-tauri/src/intelligence/prompts.rs:260` — `build_intelligence_context` (consumes entity context)
- `src-tauri/src/types.rs` or equivalent — `EntityContextEntry` shape
- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-210-plan.md` — W3-A: `AbilityRegistry`, `AbilityContext`, Read category contract
- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md` — W3-B: `AbilityOutput<T>`, `Provenance`, `SourceAttribution`
- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md` — W3-C: `intelligence_claims` (do entity context entries create claims?)
- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-299-plan.md` — W3-G: `source_asof` on user-authored content
- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-300-plan.md` — W3-H: `temporal_scope`, `sensitivity` defaults for Read ability
- `.docs/plans/wave-W4/DOS-5-plan.md` — W4-A: `TrustBand` output shape
- `.docs/plans/wave-W4/DOS-216-plan.md` — W4-B: fixture format the parity test must match
