.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4612:    13	1. **Offline evaluation.** The evaluation harness ([ADR-0107](0107-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md)) runs abilities against fixture data and captures their output and planned mutations for scoring. This is only safe if mutations are structurally impossible during the evaluation run. A mode flag that abilities check voluntarily is insufficient — any forgotten check leaks test writes into real data.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4616:    17	Today, `ServiceContext` ([ADR-0101](0101-service-boundary-enforcement.md)) carries `db`, `signals`, and `intel_queue`. It has no notion of mode and no async transaction support. Tests that need write-free runs construct their own in-memory DB; there is no consistent way to run an ability against production-anonymized fixtures in a guaranteed read-only posture.
