.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:5644:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5139:+W3-C/DOS-7 stores provenance JSON on claims and consumes `SubjectRef`, `source_asof`, and warnings; its current plan already expects W3-B to feed those fields (`.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:87`). W3-E/DOS-294 owns `FeedbackAction` and `claim_feedback`; W3-B can represent feedback as trust contributions by ID, but does not create feedback rows. W3-F/DOS-296 adds `thread_ids: Vec<ThreadId>` with `#[serde(default)]` and no schema-version bump; W3-B must not add `deny_unknown_fields` anywhere that would reject that additive field. W3-G/DOS-299 owns `source_asof` population helpers and semantic bounds; W3-B defines the field and warning carrier. W4-A/DOS-5 consumes the deterministic trust tree; W3-B does not implement numeric trust scoring.
