.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:6137:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:4089:+Do not log claim text, corrected text, notes, source excerpts, or customer names. Activity/signal rows use user-readable but bounded labels and ids; raw text stays in `claim_feedback.note` / corrected claim payload behind normal local data protections. `SurfaceInappropriate` is a privacy/sensitivity signal, not a truth contradiction, so it must not downrank the source or claim.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:6144:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:4117:+W3-B supplies `SubjectRef` / provenance source references. `WrongSubject` and `WrongSource` validation must consume those types, not parse ad hoc JSON. W3-G supplies `source_asof`; W3-H supplies claim type registry rules for `NeedsNuance` eligibility. W4 / DOS-5 consumes `claim_feedback`, `agent_trust_ledger`, and trust columns but W3-E owns the per-action semantic map that DOS-5 implements.
