.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1152:14:Without a concrete harness, these requirements do not produce action. This ADR specifies fixture structure, scoring methodology, regression classification, CI integration, and fixture governance (retention, anonymization, source-aware lifecycle).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1154:20:An evaluation fixture captures everything needed to deterministically run an ability against a known input state:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1155:24:├── fixtures/
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1156:25:│   ├── fixture_001/
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1162:34:│   ├── fixture_002/
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1166:43:Evaluation produces a score for each fixture run. Scoring differs by ability category:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1167:45:**Read abilities** — exact output equality against `expected_output.json`. Field-level diff surfaces any drift. Confidence thresholds: 100% equality required; any diff fails.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1178:85:| ProviderDrift | Warn | Inspect replay fixture; may refresh or declare as nondeterminism |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1181:93:Evaluation runs on every PR that touches `src-tauri/src/abilities/`, prompt template files, or the fixtures themselves. The harness:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1182:96:2. For each fixture in the ability's directory:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1183:97:   - Constructs `ServiceContext::new_evaluate` with the fixture's clock, seed, replay providers.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1190:121:Judge models invoke a fixture-replayed provider with a dedicated judge prompt that asks for structured rubric scores. Judge outputs are themselves subject to prompt fingerprinting and stored per run for audit.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1193:128:- **Captured from Live runs** for coverage: the `--capture-fixture` mode runs an ability in `Live` with a tracing wrapper, records everything the ability saw, and writes a fixture. Captured fixtures must be reviewed before merging.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1194:130:Fixture refresh cadence: fixtures capturing live provider output are refreshed when `prompt_template_version` changes, when the replay provider returns outdated completions, or on a quarterly schedule.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1196:134:Fixtures can contain PII and source-attributed content. Per [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) and [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md), fixtures must honor source lifecycle:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1198:138:1. Entity names replaced with placeholders (`acct_01`, `person_03`). Mapping preserved in a separate `fixture_identity_map.json` that is NOT committed.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1201:146:- Fixtures are versioned in git; historical fixtures can be reconstructed from git history.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1202:150:- When a user revokes a source, the user's `fixture_identity_map.json` (kept out-of-tree) is consulted; fixtures referencing identities mapped to revoked user data are regenerated or removed.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1203:151:- Repo-stored anonymized fixtures are not affected because the anonymization is the point of keeping them safely in-tree.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1204:153:**Multi-user note for v1.4.0 (six users, local-first):** fixtures are per-developer. Each user's captured fixtures include their own data, anonymized. No shared fixture corpus crosses users without re-anonymization.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1206:159:- Every migrated ability has at least one fixture with an expected output.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1212:177:1. **Fixture authoring is real work.** Every ability needs fixtures before it can be gated.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1214:180:4. **Fixture drift from production data.** Fixtures capture point-in-time state; real-world drift means fixtures require periodic refresh.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1216:185:2. **Anonymization bugs leak PII into fixtures.** Mitigation: anonymization is reviewed; pre-commit hook grep for known-PII patterns (phone numbers, email patterns not matching `@example.com`).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1217:186:3. **Fixture rot.** Abilities evolve; fixtures don't. Mitigation: every ability version bump requires fixture review; fixtures older than quarterly cadence trigger CI advisory.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1218:187:4. **CI runtime ballooning.** Many fixtures × many abilities = long test time. Mitigation: parallel execution; fixture labels (`@core`, `@regression`, `@edge`) allow selective PR-time subsets with full suite on nightly runs.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1219:188:5. **Fixture identity map loss.** `fixture_identity_map.json` lost means purge-on-revocation cannot target specific fixtures. Mitigation: identity map is backed up per-developer; reconstruction from git history plus user-side records is possible but manual.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1221:192:Every scaffold in the harness — dimension split, consistency-repair retry budget, PTY concurrency caps, multi-step fan-out — encodes an assumption about what the model can't do alone on current hardware with current prompts. Those assumptions go stale as models improve. This amendment adds a fixture class that periodically tests whether named harness components still earn their keep.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1222:194:### 9.1 Stripped-harness fixture class
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1223:196:A new optional field on the fixture manifest:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1224:199:[fixture_001]
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1225:200:strip = ["dimension_split"]   # Disable this harness component during the fixture run
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1226:211:Multiple strips per fixture are permitted. The harness records the strip set in the run metadata so regressions are attributable to the removed scaffold.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1227:213:### 9.2 Scoring stripped fixtures
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1228:215:Stripped fixtures are scored by the same rubric as their unstripped counterparts (§5 `quality.toml` thresholds). The harness records both the stripped and unstripped composite scores on a schedule — **quarterly** by default, configurable per ability.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1230:225:Stripped fixtures run on a schedule, not on every PR. Strip deltas are informational — they do not fail builds. A material finding (`strip_delta ≤ 0.02` across three quarterly cycles) opens a follow-on issue tagged `harness-retirement-candidate` for engineering review. Retirement is a conscious decision, not an automatic response.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1232:237:3. At least one fixture opting into that strip.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1233:247:- [ADR-0104: ExecutionMode and Mode-Aware Services](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md) — `Evaluate` mode enables hermetic evaluation; fixtures consumed via `ServiceContext::new_evaluate`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1234:248:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — Expected provenance is part of every fixture; attribution accuracy gauged via LLM self-eval.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1266:86:**Replay is keyed by `canonical_prompt_hash`, not by seed.** A replay provider's fixture maps `canonical_prompt_hash → Completion`. Looking up a completion by hash gives the fixture's recorded response. If the hash is missing from the fixture, the replay provider returns `Error::FixtureMissingCompletion { hash }`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1267:88:**Seed is for live generation determinism, not replay.** When `Evaluate` mode drives a live provider (e.g., running a regression test against a real model to capture a new fixture), `seed` is mandatory; the provider passes it through to the model API. When `Evaluate` mode drives a replay provider, `seed` is retained in the fingerprint for audit but does not drive the replay.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1268:90:**Fixture construction.** Running an ability in `Live` mode with a tracing wrapper records every provider invocation (prompt template ID, inputs, metadata, completion). The captured sequence is the replay fixture for future `Evaluate` runs. [ADR-0110](0110-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md) specifies fixture storage, anonymization, and refresh cadence.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1271:110:- Same inputs, same `prompt_template_version`, different outputs → provider drift or fixture inconsistency
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1283:138:5. **Replay fixture staleness.** Live provider behavior drifts from fixture. Mitigation: fixtures are refreshed on a declared cadence. Staleness is flagged at evaluation time when a replay produces unexpected outputs vs. a live spot-check.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1286:145:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — §1 `PromptFingerprint` shape referenced; this ADR provides the definition.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1292:13:1. **Offline evaluation.** The evaluation harness ([ADR-0107](0107-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md)) runs abilities against fixture data and captures their output and planned mutations for scoring. This is only safe if mutations are structurally impossible during the evaluation run. A mode flag that abilities check voluntarily is insufficient — any forgotten check leaks test writes into real data.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1294:17:Today, `ServiceContext` ([ADR-0101](0101-service-boundary-enforcement.md)) carries `db`, `signals`, and `intel_queue`. It has no notion of mode and no async transaction support. Tests that need write-free runs construct their own in-memory DB; there is no consistent way to run an ability against production-anonymized fixtures in a guaranteed read-only posture.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1313:74:Each `*Wrapper` respects `ExecutionMode`: in `Live`, it calls the real client; in `Simulate` or `Evaluate`, it consults the replay fixture supplied during construction (per `ServiceContext::new_simulate`/`new_evaluate`). Abilities access external services exclusively through `ctx.services.external.glean.*`, `ctx.services.external.slack.*`, etc. The `AbilityContext` does not hold any external client reference directly — that would bypass mode-aware routing.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1316:91:        external: ExternalClients<'a>,  // fixture-backed replay wrappers
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1319:104:- `new_simulate` takes fixture-backed external wrappers and a tracer-only signal sink.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1320:105:- `new_evaluate` internally constructs `ExternalClients` from the `EvalFixture`'s replay data; the caller does not provide them separately. The fixture also supplies the deterministic clock and seeded RNG.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1345:207:**External calls are mode-aware.** Services that call external APIs (Glean, Slack, Gmail, Salesforce) check mode at the call boundary and route to either the live client (`Live`) or a replay fixture supplied by the `EvalFixture` (`Simulate`/`Evaluate`). The replay fixture API is specified in [ADR-0107](0107-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1346:209:**Intelligence provider is mode-aware via injection.** In `Live`, `AbilityContext.intelligence` is the production provider. In `Simulate`/`Evaluate`, it is a replay provider constructed from the `EvalFixture` and matched by prompt hash. The provider interface ([ADR-0091](0091-intelligence-provider-abstraction.md)) is the same; only the implementation differs per mode.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1351:243:`ExecutionMode` is set by the **surface** that constructs `ServiceContext` and propagates through `AbilityContext` to any ability invoked in that request. Abilities cannot change the mode. Surfaces:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1355:251:| Developer simulation REPL / dev tooling | `Simulate` | Never — `Simulate` is a developer-mode affordance (stubbed providers, replay fixtures) not intended for user-facing flows |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1356:254:Inside a running invocation, mode is immutable. An ability that invokes another ability passes the same `AbilityContext`; the child ability sees the same mode as the parent.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1359:260:- **Clock.** `ctx.clock.now()` returns fixture-supplied timestamps, not the system clock. All abilities and services read time via the injected clock, never via `chrono::Utc::now()` directly.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1360:261:- **RNG.** `ctx.rng.gen()` returns deterministic values from a fixture-supplied seed. Abilities that sample (e.g., stochastic health scoring in [ADR-0097](0097-account-health-scoring-architecture.md)) use the injected RNG.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1371:303:- `ServiceContext::new_evaluate` and fixture wiring enable the evaluation harness ([ADR-0107](0107-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md)).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1379:328:4. **External-call routing adds a mode branch to every integration.** Glean, Slack, Gmail, Salesforce wrappers each gain a mode check and a fixture replay path.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1383:337:5. **Mode confusion in integration tests.** A test runs Simulate when it needs Live, or vice versa, and silently passes without actually testing the mutation path. Mitigation: test-mode declaration is explicit; integration tests that need Live mutations declare so in their fixture setup.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1386:346:3. **Determinism for DB-level defaults and triggers.** SQLite `DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` columns and triggers that compute timestamps bypass the injected clock. `Evaluate` mode cannot fully deterministically reproduce runs if the schema relies on DB-side clocks. Mitigation: the schema audit performed in Phase 2 migrates any DB-side clock usage to service-layer clock injection. Migration ticket tracked separately; until complete, fixtures may see timestamp drift on re-run, which the snapshot-diff scorer tolerates via a small field-level ignore list.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1388:348:5. **Provider and external-client wiring.** `ServiceContext` holds mode-aware external clients via `ExternalClients` (§2). `IntelligenceProvider` is held on `AbilityContext` rather than `ServiceContext` because multiple providers may co-exist (different abilities can use different providers), whereas external API clients are scoped to the service layer and share replay fixtures. `ServiceContext::new_simulate` and `new_evaluate` wire the mode-appropriate `ExternalClients` wrappers that route to replay fixtures. The surface (app, MCP, worker, harness) wires the mode-appropriate `IntelligenceProvider` into the `AbilityContext` it constructs. This split is intentional: externals are mode-routed by the service layer; provider selection is per-ability concern owned by the surface.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1390:354:- [ADR-0102: Abilities as the Runtime Contract](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) — Consumes `AbilityContext` which wraps `ServiceContext` with its mode. §5 and §11 of that ADR require the contract established here.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1392:357:- [ADR-0091: IntelligenceProvider Abstraction](0091-intelligence-provider-abstraction.md) — Evaluate mode requires a replay variant of `IntelligenceProvider` supplied by the fixture.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1393:358:- **ADR-0107 (forthcoming): Evaluation Harness for Abilities** — Consumes `ExecutionMode::Evaluate` and specifies fixture structure, replay semantics, and snapshot-diff scoring.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1409:.docs/decisions/0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md:41:### Principle 1: Persist Locally, Tag Provenance
