.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1432:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:120:When rendering exceeds a budget, the renderer truncates deepest-first (children elided first, sources last) and surfaces a `ProvenanceWarning::TruncatedForRender { surface, budget_bytes, original_bytes }`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1433:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:148:4. **Masking has explicit shape.** `ProvenanceMasked` is defined; consumers handle `ProvenanceOrMasked` uniformly.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1435:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:169:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — Defines the envelope; this ADR specifies rendering.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1436:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:173:- [ADR-0103: Maintenance Ability Safety Constraints](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) — `MaintenanceAuditRecord` carries `ProvenanceOrMasked` per this ADR's §4.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1437:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:186:- The cap applies to the full `Provenance` envelope after JSON serialization, before any surface rendering.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1438:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:187:- Abilities that would exceed the cap return `Err(AbilityError::ProvenanceTooLarge { size_bytes, cap_bytes })`. No silent truncation.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1439:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:188:- The cap is enforced at `AbilityOutput<T>` construction time. The error surfaces to the caller as a hard error (per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) error-handling amendment).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1440:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:192:1. **Provenance summarization** — collapse deep composition trees into summary nodes marked `ProvenanceWarning::DepthElided`. [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1 already declares this warning class; this amendment activates it.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1443:.docs/decisions/0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md:131:The `scoring_class` field on `SourceAttribution` ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §4) is derived from this table, not author-set. Consumers that aggregate sources for scoring filter by class to avoid conflating Slack chatter with Salesforce ARR.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1446:.docs/decisions/0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md:174:- Reading a synthesized field populates `SourceAttribution.synthesis_marker` so the trust builder sees it.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1448:.docs/decisions/0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md:209:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — §4 `SourceAttribution` uses this ADR's `DataSource` and `SourceIdentifier`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1449:.docs/decisions/0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md:210:- [ADR-0108: Provenance Rendering and Privacy](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) — Renders masking behavior and flag-for-re-enrichment status.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1450:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:1:# ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1452:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:13:[ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §9 Rule 5 declares that every ability output carries provenance via `AbilityOutput<T>`. §10 declares Transform outputs are untrusted for mutation authorization. §11.3 declares composition produces nested provenance trees. [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 requires maintenance audit records to carry provenance. All of these contracts depend on one shape: the `Provenance` envelope. ADR-0102 references it but does not specify it.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1454:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:19:Every ability output carries a `Provenance` envelope via the `AbilityOutput<T>` wrapper from [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §6. The envelope captures identity, temporal context, trust classification, source attribution, composition tree, and field-level attribution.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1455:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:21:### 1. The Provenance Envelope
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1456:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:24:pub struct Provenance {
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1460:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:46:    pub sources: Vec<SourceAttribution>,
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1461:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:52:    pub children: Vec<Provenance>,
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1463:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:58:    pub warnings: Vec<ProvenanceWarning>,
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1464:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:61:pub enum ProvenanceWarning {
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1468:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:135:    DirectSource { index: usize },         // Points into Provenance.sources
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1469:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:136:    ComposedChild { index: usize },        // Points into Provenance.children
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1470:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:158:**`effective` is computed by the provenance builder, not the author.** The author cannot set it; the registry rejects manually-constructed `Provenance` with mismatched `effective` and `contributions`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1471:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:165:pub struct SourceAttribution {
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1472:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:169:    pub source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,      // When the source itself was authored (if known)
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1473:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:237:1. Every field in the ability's domain output MUST have an entry in `field_attributions`. No "optional for Read" escape hatch — Read abilities' fields are typically `Direct` with `ConfidenceKind::Implicit`, which is trivial to populate but must exist.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1474:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:248:Provenance(A) {
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1475:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:250:  children: [Provenance(B), Provenance(C), ...],
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1479:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:264:6. Cycle guard: the registry rejects ability composition cycles at registration time per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §11.1, so nested `Provenance` trees are guaranteed acyclic.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1480:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:268:### 7. Provenance Builder Pattern
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1481:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:277:    let mut prov = ProvenanceBuilder::new(ctx, "prepare_meeting");
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1483:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:310:- Wraps the domain output in `AbilityOutput<T>` with the built provenance.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1484:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:315:Provenance persists anywhere the ability output is stored. Specifically:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1485:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:317:1. **Maintenance audit table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 `MaintenanceAuditRecord` adds a `provenance: Provenance` field. Source revocation triggers a masking pass: a `Provenance` whose sources reference a revoked `DataSource` is replaced with a `ProvenanceMasked` marker per [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md). **Interaction with [ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md):** ADR-0094's append-only JSONL security audit remains unchanged. The `maintenance_audit` SQLite table is a separate operational log for runtime diagnostics. Provenance content in the operational log is subject to masking; the JSONL security log is unchanged.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1486:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:319:2. **Outbox table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §2 outbox entries add a `provenance: Provenance` field. Outbox provenance captures the ability's full output-time provenance, including the invocation that generated the pending external mutation.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1487:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:325:**Storage format.** Provenance is stored as JSON in a single column per containing record. Indexes on `invocation_id`, `ability_name`, `produced_at`, and `data_source` (via a normalized xref table) support the queries [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 requires. A full JSON-column approach is feasible at the six-user scale; if scale changes, a normalized `provenance` / `provenance_sources` split can be introduced without changing the envelope contract.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1488:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:333:**Hard truncation.** When a provenance envelope exceeds 1MB at finalize time, composition subtrees are collapsed from deepest first into a `ProvenanceWarning::DepthElided` summary carrying aggregate source counts and trust classification. Truncation is a finalize-time concern; the full tree never leaves the ability in its raw form above the hard limit.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1489:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:341:3. **Scoped reproducibility.** The `InputsSnapshot` supports staleness detection, diff reasoning, and fixture-mode replay — the three use cases that actually matter — without overpromising exact content-level replay of live runs.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1490:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:343:5. **Source revocation can cascade correctly.** Provenance references `DataSource` via [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md), and lifecycle behavior (purge vs. flag) is governed by that ADR. Masking shape is governed by [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1491:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:348:1. **Every ability pays an authoring cost.** Provenance building is part of the ability's job. Contributors must think about source attribution when writing synthesis.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1492:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:349:2. **Provenance can be large.** Deep composition with full field attribution produces substantial JSON. Soft budget warns; hard truncation bounds worst-case.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1493:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:357:3. **Storage volume growth.** Provenance retained indefinitely alongside outputs accumulates. Mitigation: same retention as output; no separate provenance retention policy.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1495:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:364:- [ADR-0102: Abilities as the Runtime Contract](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) — Defines `AbilityOutput<T>` wrapper; §9 Rule 5 requires provenance; §10 consumes `TrustAssessment`; §11.3 requires composition merge.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1496:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:365:- [ADR-0103: Maintenance Ability Safety Constraints](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) — §8 maintenance audit records add a `provenance: Provenance` field per §8 of this ADR.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1497:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:371:- **[ADR-0108: Provenance Rendering and Privacy](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md)** — Per-surface rendering rules, actor-filtered display, `ProvenanceMasked` shape, sanitization of `explanation` text, and P2 publication safety.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1500:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:379:## Amendment — 2026-04-24 — `source_asof` population semantics + `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1501:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:383:The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md` §10) identified that `source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` exists in §4 above as optional metadata but no code path actually populates it. Today's storage path stamps `observed_at = now` (`glean_provider.rs:1182`) regardless of when the underlying source was authored. The Glean/PTY prompts ask for `sourcedAt` per item (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`) but the returned timestamp lives in a JSON blob and is never lifted into the first-class column.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1502:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391:`source_asof` is amended from "optional metadata" to **must-be-populated-when-knowable**, with an explicit population chain:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1503:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:394:populate(source_asof) = pick first available:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1504:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401:If all four fail, `source_asof = None` AND the Provenance envelope emits a new warning variant:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1505:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:404:pub enum ProvenanceWarning {
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1506:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:427:freshness_input_age = match (source_asof, observed_at):
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1507:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:435:### C. `ProvenanceBuilder` enforcement
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1508:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:437:The builder lifts `itemSource.sourcedAt` (when present in LLM output) and Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` automatically. Authors do not manually populate the field. The builder emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` when the population chain falls to step 4.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1509:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:443:| DOS-211 (Provenance Builder, spine) | Builder lifts `sourcedAt` from `itemSource` JSON or Glean document metadata into `source_asof`. Emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning on full fallback. |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1510:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:446:| DOS-218 / DOS-219 (pilot abilities, spine) | Acceptance criteria include: produces ≥1 claim with `source_asof` populated and ≥1 claim with `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning, demonstrating the chain works both ways. |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1511:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:447:| `glean_provider.rs:1182` write path | Lift Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` before writing SignalEvent / claim row. Don't stamp `observed_at = now` as the only timestamp. |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1512:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:452:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1513:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:457:backfill source_asof for each migrated claim:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1514:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:459:     → source_asof = parsed timestamp
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1515:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:461:     → source_asof = None AND emit ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampUnknown { fallback: ObservedAt }
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1516:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:472:The migration applies these bounds to every parsed `source_asof`:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1517:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:481:    → mark claim with ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampImplausible { reason: "before entity origin" }
