.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:321:    /// → consumes the typed `SubjectRef` from ADR-0105 SubjectAttribution amendment.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:322:    WrongSubject { corrected_to: Option<SubjectRef> },
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:365:    pub subject: SubjectRef,                  // From ADR-0105 SubjectAttribution amendment
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:416:`WrongSubject { corrected_to }` is the user-side complement to ADR-0105's `SubjectAttribution` substrate primitive. Behavior:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:419:- `corrected_to: Some(SubjectRef)` — "this content belongs to that entity instead." Tombstone at the asserted subject; propose (not commit) a new claim at the corrected subject with the same claim_text, full provenance preserved, `actor = 'user_correction'`. The corrected claim enters via the standard propose/commit path so it gets the same gate as any other claim.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:429:3. Job invokes a `find_corroborating_evidence` Read ability (lands in v1.4.1; v1.4.0 ships the queue + skeleton).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:441:- `find_corroborating_evidence` Read ability — v1.4.1; v1.4.0 ships the queue + skeleton.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:449:- `WrongSubject` becomes a substrate-level operation pairing cleanly with ADR-0105 `SubjectAttribution`. Subject mistakes do not punish sources.
