.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:978:3. **Eval reproducibility under fixtures.** In `Evaluate` mode, the fixture's state is deterministic; the snapshot plus the fixture reconstructs the run. [ADR-0110](0110-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md) (forthcoming — renumbered from 0107) specifies how.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:980:**Reproducibility is a scoped claim, not an unqualified one.** Full content-level replay of non-fixture runs is not promised and is out of scope for this ADR.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:995:    /// True if any ancestor (Read or otherwise) returned content that was
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:997:    /// category is Read. Closes the "stored AI output laundering" hole.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1016:    DirectSource { index: usize },         // Points into Provenance.sources
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1017:    ComposedChild { index: usize },        // Points into Provenance.children
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1025:    StoredSynthesis,                       // Read ability exposed a stored LLM-synthesized value
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1037:**This closes the laundering hole.** A Read ability that returns stored AI output (e.g., a cached `entity_assessment.summary` from Glean) is `Untrusted` because the stored field itself carries a synthesis marker. The `contains_stored_synthesis` flag and `TrustReason::StoredSynthesis` contribution make the reasoning explicit.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1039:**`effective` is computed by the provenance builder, not the author.** The author cannot set it; the registry rejects manually-constructed `Provenance` with mismatched `effective` and `contributions`.
