.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1528:.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:148:`WrongSubject { corrected_to }` is the user-side complement to ADR-0105's `SubjectAttribution` substrate primitive. Behavior:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1530:.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:151:- `corrected_to: Some(SubjectRef)` — "this content belongs to that entity instead." Tombstone at the asserted subject; propose (not commit) a new claim at the corrected subject with the same claim_text, full provenance preserved, `actor = 'user_correction'`. The corrected claim enters via the standard propose/commit path so it gets the same gate as any other claim.
