.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1536:.docs/plans/wave-W2/reviews/DOS-259-l0-code-reviewer-v3.md:37:- §4 (Security, line 85): "Evaluate-mode replay routing is structurally enforced via the AbilityContext-bearing factory plus the ADR-0091 AppState `Arc`-swap pattern." This is the load-bearing security invariant for Evaluate, and it is consistent with the §3 ownership model. The Live/Evaluate/Simulate routing in §3 line 77 ("Live returns the configured AppState provider `Arc`, Evaluate returns replay, and Simulate returns a non-live provider whose `complete()` fails closed with `ProviderError::ModeNotSupported`") matches §4's structural-enforcement claim.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1542:.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-310-plan.md:13:- Spine restriction enforced at CLAIM_TYPE_REGISTRY layer (no claim_type registers `canonical_subject_types: &[SubjectType::Global]`), NOT at `SubjectRef::Global` construction. `Global` IS structurally available.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1547:.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-310-plan.md:50:5. **Tests:** Multi sorted-lock test (concurrent claim writes affecting overlapping entity sets do not deadlock); per-entity claim_version bump verified for each entity type; Global subject restriction verified at compile time via trybuild fixture.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1582:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:23:Schema in the migration: `intelligence_claims` with immutable assertion columns (`id`, `subject_ref`, `claim_type`, `field_path` or `topic_key`, `text`, `dedup_key`, `item_hash`, `actor`, `data_source`, `source_ref`, `source_asof`, `observed_at`, `created_at`, `provenance_json`, `metadata_json`), lifecycle columns (`claim_state`, `surfacing_state`, `demotion_reason`, `reactivated_at`, `retraction_reason`, `expires_at`, `superseded_by`, `trust_score`, `trust_computed_at`, `trust_version`, `thread_id`, `temporal_scope`, `sensitivity`), and indexes for default reads plus suppression lookup. Include `thread_id` from ADR-0124 (`.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:33-48`), `source_asof` from ADR-0105 (`.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391-466`), and `temporal_scope` / `sensitivity` from ADR-0125 (`.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:51-87`) in the initial create-table if W3-C lands first, to avoid later ALTER churn.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1584:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:37:Keep the table. Deriving from Provenance envelopes fails the product contract: it cannot enforce a synchronous tombstone PRE-GATE, cannot answer "all claims about subject X" without replaying historical ability outputs, cannot carry user feedback and repair jobs as first-class targets, and cannot preserve 9 legacy dismissal sources under one immutable identity. Provenance becomes `provenance_json` plus source/corroboration rows, not the storage root.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1587:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:61:Hot paths: enrichment suppression filtering (`src-tauri/src/intel_queue.rs:2375-2403`), claim default reads, `commit_claim`, corroboration writes, and the one-time 9-mechanism backfill. The covering suppression index should support `(subject_ref, claim_type, field_path, claim_state, dedup_key, item_hash, expires_at, source_asof)` or equivalent; default reads need `(subject_ref, claim_state, surfacing_state, claim_type)`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1605:.docs/plans/wave-W2/reviews/DOS-209-l0-codex-consult-v2.md:32:Confidence comes from the concrete W2-A implementation spine in `DOS-209-plan.md` §2-§4 and §9: `services/context.rs` ownership, exact carrier/visibility rules, `ServiceError` variants, `with_transaction_async` signature plus fallback, exhaustive mutator catalogue, surface-constructor test, mutation-catalog structural lint, mode-boundary runtime test, clock/RNG lint, and capability trybuild fixtures.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1615:.docs/decisions/0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md:219:Codex round 2 finding 13 surfaced that the v1.4.0 spine plan (DOS-299) needed to preserve item-level confidence semantics for legacy items without `ItemSource` (the current `HasSource::effective_confidence` defaults missing source to `0.5` per `intelligence/io.rs:1185-1189`). My earlier writeup proposed registering this in the `CLAIM_TYPE_REGISTRY` (per ADR-0125). That was wrong — it's a `DataSource` taxonomy concern, not a claim type. ADR-0107 owns `DataSource`; this amendment adds the variant.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1620:.docs/decisions/0126-memory-substrate-invariants.md:22:Once a claim is written, its `text`, `claim_type`, `subject_ref`, `source_asof`, and `created_at` are immutable. No UPDATE of those columns from anywhere in the codebase except migration paths.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1621:.docs/decisions/0126-memory-substrate-invariants.md:101:- **source** — a DataSource variant (DOS-212) with `source_asof`
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1622:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:169:    pub source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,      // When the source itself was authored (if known)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1623:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:379:## Amendment — 2026-04-24 — `source_asof` population semantics + `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1624:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:383:The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md` §10) identified that `source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` exists in §4 above as optional metadata but no code path actually populates it. Today's storage path stamps `observed_at = now` (`glean_provider.rs:1182`) regardless of when the underlying source was authored. The Glean/PTY prompts ask for `sourcedAt` per item (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`) but the returned timestamp lives in a JSON blob and is never lifted into the first-class column.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1625:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391:`source_asof` is amended from "optional metadata" to **must-be-populated-when-knowable**, with an explicit population chain:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1626:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:394:populate(source_asof) = pick first available:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1628:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401:If all four fail, `source_asof = None` AND the Provenance envelope emits a new warning variant:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1629:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:427:freshness_input_age = match (source_asof, observed_at):
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1630:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:437:The builder lifts `itemSource.sourcedAt` (when present in LLM output) and Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` automatically. Authors do not manually populate the field. The builder emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` when the population chain falls to step 4.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1631:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:443:| DOS-211 (Provenance Builder, spine) | Builder lifts `sourcedAt` from `itemSource` JSON or Glean document metadata into `source_asof`. Emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning on full fallback. |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1632:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:446:| DOS-218 / DOS-219 (pilot abilities, spine) | Acceptance criteria include: produces ≥1 claim with `source_asof` populated and ≥1 claim with `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning, demonstrating the chain works both ways. |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1633:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:447:| `glean_provider.rs:1182` write path | Lift Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` before writing SignalEvent / claim row. Don't stamp `observed_at = now` as the only timestamp. |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1635:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:452:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1636:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:457:backfill source_asof for each migrated claim:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1638:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:459:     → source_asof = parsed timestamp
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1640:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:461:     → source_asof = None AND emit ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampUnknown { fallback: ObservedAt }
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1642:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:472:The migration applies these bounds to every parsed `source_asof`:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1643:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:483:  - timestamp > now + 30 days (near-future; legitimate for renewal dates but suspicious for source_asof)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1644:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:498:- Auto-classifier for inferring `source_asof` from claim_text content (v1.5.x+).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1645:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:499:- Backfill of `source_asof` from sources OTHER than existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` (e.g., re-fetching Glean documents to recover their timestamps for old claims). This is post-spine cleanup if needed.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1646:.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md:5:**Why now:** SubjectAttribution (this morning), ThreadId (this afternoon), and recency / `source_asof` (later this afternoon) all surfaced as substrate gaps reactively. Each was real. The pattern suggests there are more. Cheap to enumerate before code starts; expensive after.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1647:.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md:27:`source_refs`, `prompt_fingerprint`, `synthesis_marker`. ADR-0105 §4. **Note: §10 below amends `source_asof` semantics; the field exists, the population path doesn't.**
