.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1726:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1238:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2407:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:383:The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md` §10) identified that `source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` exists in §4 above as optional metadata but no code path actually populates it. Today's storage path stamps `observed_at = now` (`glean_provider.rs:1182`) regardless of when the underlying source was authored. The Glean/PTY prompts ask for `sourcedAt` per item (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`) but the returned timestamp lives in a JSON blob and is never lifted into the first-class column.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1727:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1239:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2408:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391:`source_asof` is amended from "optional metadata" to **must-be-populated-when-knowable**, with an explicit population chain:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1728:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1240:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2409:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:394:populate(source_asof) = pick first available:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1729:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1241:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2410:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401:If all four fail, `source_asof = None` AND the Provenance envelope emits a new warning variant:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1730:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1242:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2411:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:427:freshness_input_age = match (source_asof, observed_at):
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1731:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1243:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2412:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:437:The builder lifts `itemSource.sourcedAt` (when present in LLM output) and Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` automatically. Authors do not manually populate the field. The builder emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` when the population chain falls to step 4.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1732:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1244:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2413:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:443:| DOS-211 (Provenance Builder, spine) | Builder lifts `sourcedAt` from `itemSource` JSON or Glean document metadata into `source_asof`. Emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning on full fallback. |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1733:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1245:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2414:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:446:| DOS-218 / DOS-219 (pilot abilities, spine) | Acceptance criteria include: produces ≥1 claim with `source_asof` populated and ≥1 claim with `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning, demonstrating the chain works both ways. |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1734:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1246:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2415:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:447:| `glean_provider.rs:1182` write path | Lift Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` before writing SignalEvent / claim row. Don't stamp `observed_at = now` as the only timestamp. |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:1735:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:1247:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:2416:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:452:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
